From: Jerome Berclaz <26882162+jberclaz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: tegra: use a direct call to power off a dying CPU

tegra_cpu_die() disables the data cache and leaves SMP coherency, then
calls the SoC's shutdown routine through the tegra_hotplug_shutdown
function pointer. On the Microsoft Surface RT (Tegra 30, Cortex-A9
r2p9) booted through U-Boot, that indirect call hangs the dying CPU: it
never reaches the flow-controller writes in tegra30_cpu_shutdown(), so
every CPU offline, and with it every suspend, hangs the system.

Reading the pointer before the cache is disabled does not help; a direct
branch does. Decide which routine to call while the cache is still on
and branch to it directly. The LP2 cpuidle path already reaches
tegra30_cpu_shutdown() through direct branches from assembly and does
not hang.

Tested on a Surface RT, kernel 7.3.1 (libre-tegra eab1ff1e), U-Boot RAM
boot, together with "ARM: tegra: mask imprecise aborts before disabling
the data cache": 10 rounds of taking cpu1-3 offline and online, and 5
consecutive "deep" (LP2) suspend/resume cycles, both with cpuidle off
and with cpuidle (C7/CC6) enabled.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-tegra/hotplug.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-tegra/hotplug.c
@@ -37,16 +37,29 @@
  */
 void tegra_cpu_die(unsigned int cpu)
 {
+	bool t20;
+
 	if (!tegra_hotplug_shutdown) {
 		WARN(1, "hotplug is not yet initialized\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* Decide while the data cache is still on. */
+	t20 = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_TEGRA_2x_SOC) &&
+	      tegra_hotplug_shutdown == tegra20_hotplug_shutdown;
+
 	/* Clean L1 data cache */
 	tegra_disable_clean_inv_dcache(TEGRA_FLUSH_CACHE_LOUIS);
 
-	/* Shut down the current CPU. */
-	tegra_hotplug_shutdown();
+	/*
+	 * Shut down the current CPU with a direct branch: the data cache is
+	 * off and this CPU has left coherency, and the indirect call through
+	 * tegra_hotplug_shutdown hangs the Microsoft Surface RT here.
+	 */
+	if (t20)
+		tegra20_hotplug_shutdown();
+	else
+		tegra30_hotplug_shutdown();
 
 	/* Should never return here. */
 	BUG();
